<h2 id="section-1">Start with the SUIJI system rule</h2>
<p>Every SUIJI ornament fits every jewelry base equipped with the SUIJI multi-use clasp. The ornament gives the piece its look; the base holds it in place and makes it wearable. You can keep an ornament you love and choose a different equipped base, or keep your base and change the ornament.</p>
<p>The useful first question is which parts you already have. A bare hoop, a connector, a completed base with Core-Lock and an ornament are different things. A photograph of an assembled piece may show more than the product listing includes. Check the included-parts list before choosing an addition.</p>
<h2 id="section-2">Make a three-part check</h2>
<div class="sj-table-scroll" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="SUIJI component checklist"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Check</th><th scope="col">What to identify</th><th scope="col">What it tells you</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Your base</td><td>The reference and whether the SUIJI multi-use clasp is included</td><td>Whether it is already a completed base for the ornament system</td></tr><tr><td>Your ornament</td><td>The exact decorative element and whether one or a pair is supplied</td><td>Which look you are choosing and how many wearing positions it can fill</td></tr><tr><td>Additional parts</td><td>Any base or attachment listed as separate</td><td>What you still need for the composition shown</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>For example, the H01 hoop on its own does not include Core-Lock. A completed arrangement can use a separate attachment and clasp-equipped base. The extra component has a job; it is not another ornament. Follow the actual component names and contents rather than assuming that a hoop and a finished interchangeable earring are the same product.</p>
<h2 id="section-3">Count shared ornaments once</h2>
<p>A base with two ornaments gives you two choices to wear in turn. S03 contains one ring base and two ornaments, not two complete rings. S04 contains two hoops, two pendant bases, two ornaments and one necklace. The same two ornaments are shared between arrangements.</p>
<p>S06 adds a ring base to the S04 contents and still has two ornaments. Three possible wearing positions do not create three fully decorated pieces at the same time. Write down the look you want to wear now, then allocate each ornament to one position. This simple count helps you see whether an extra ornament would be useful.</p>
<h2 id="section-4">Keep the distinction useful</h2>
<p>The SUIJI system rule applies to SUIJI ornaments and bases equipped with the SUIJI multi-use clasp. It does not establish a fit with a third-party base or an unrelated closure. Do not force, bend or enlarge a connection to make a different system fit.</p>
<p>If a name or photograph does not identify the base clearly, ask for the reference and included components. You do not need to reopen the compatibility rule for every SUIJI ornament; you need to establish that the piece in front of you is the equipped base or attachment described.</p>
<h2 id="section-5">Useful questions</h2>
<h3>Does every SUIJI hoop include Core-Lock?</h3><p>No. The product’s included-parts list tells you whether a clasp or a separate attachment is supplied. The H01 hoop on its own is distinct from a completed clasp-equipped arrangement.</p>
<h3>Do I need a new base for every ornament?</h3><p>No. Keep a base equipped with the SUIJI multi-use clasp and change the SUIJI ornament. Choose another base when you want a different wearing position or another complete piece.</p>
<h3>Can I wear all the set photographs at once?</h3><p>Check the ornament count. Several photographs may show the same ornaments moved between bases. Shared components are counted once in the included list.</p>
<h3>What should I ask when I cannot identify a part?</h3><p>Try: “I have base reference A and would like this arrangement. Which components are included, and is another attachment required?” A clear reference is more useful than guessing from a similar-looking photograph.</p>
<h2 id="section-6">Your next step</h2>
<p>List your base, the ornaments and any separate attachment. Then <a href="{% render 'suiji-localized-menu-url', url: '/pages/the-mechanism' %}">explore how the SUIJI system works</a> or <a href="{% render 'suiji-localized-menu-url', url: '/collections/sets' %}">compare the complete sets</a>.</p>
